+//! Endgame successor filters (`SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME`).
+//!
+//! Reference model / authority for the semantics ported here:
+//! `tools/verify_endgame.py`, functions `f_bound1_unique` and `f_halving`
+//! (E1, E2). The third filter (E3/E4, "live support") was corrected mid-patch
+//! from an earlier "dirty channel / unsettled pair" conjecture that could not
+//! be proven; see [`live_support`]'s doc comment for the proof actually used.
+//!
+//! # Soundness of the gate
+//!
+//! Every filter here is only consulted when the *parent* state's stored
+//! upper bound `b = state.bounds[1]` is `<= SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME_BUDGET`
+//! (default 4). `b` is always a sound upper bound on `bound(X)` (never
+//! required to be tight). If the true value is `m <= b`, any optimal
+//! successor `Y` has `bound(Y) = m - 1 <= b - 1`, so a test parameterised by
+//! `b - 1` can never exclude every optimal successor. This is why every
+//! filter function below takes the *parent's* `b`, not `bound(X)` itself,
+//! which the engine does not know exactly.
+//!
+//! # Filters
+//!
+//! * **E1** ([`bound1_unique_pair`]): when `b == 1` and `X` is not sorted,
+//!   `bound(X)` is exactly 1 (see the gate reasoning above plus the note in
+//!   `search.rs` on why `state.bounds[0] >= 1` for every unsorted state), and
+//!   the sorting comparator is uniquely determined by `X`'s Hamming-weight
+//!   class structure. When the theorem's structural precondition holds, the
+//!   whole `i, j` double loop `Search::improve` normally runs can be replaced
+//!   by trying that one pair.
+//! * **E2** ([`halving_ok`]): a comparator is at most 2-to-1 within each
+//!   Hamming weight class, so `bound(X) >= ceil(log2 max_l |X_l|)`. A
+//!   successor `Y` is admissible only if `max_l |Y_l| <= 2^(b-1)`.
+//! * **E3/E4** ([`live_support`], [`live_budget_ok`]): the *live support*
+//!   `L(Z)` is the set of channels on which two vectors of **equal Hamming
+//!   weight** in `Z` disagree. Every channel in `L(Z)` must be touched by
+//!   some comparator of any network sorting `Z` (proof below), and each
+//!   comparator touches exactly 2 channels, so `bound(Z) >= ceil(|L(Z)| / 2)`.
+//!   A successor `Y` is admissible only if `|L(Y)| <= 2 * (b - 1)`.
+//!
+//!   Proof that every channel of `L(Z)` is touched: comparator networks
+//!   preserve Hamming weight, and `OutputSet::is_sorted` accepts `Z` iff `Z`
+//!   has at most one vector per weight. Suppose network `N` never touches
+//!   channel `p`; then `N(v)_p = v_p` for every `v`. Take `u, v` in `Z` of
+//!   equal weight with `u_p != v_p` (this is exactly what `p in L(Z)`
+//!   means); `N(u)` and `N(v)` then have equal weight too, so if `N(Z)` is
+//!   sorted, `N(u) = N(v)` -- but they still disagree at channel `p` (`N`
+//!   left it alone), a contradiction. So every channel of `L(Z)` is touched
+//!   by every sorting network for `Z`, hence by some comparator of it.
+//!
+//! Composite policy (mirrors `verify_endgame.py`'s `f_e1_e2_e4`): at `b == 1`
+//! only E1 applies (and replaces enumeration entirely); at `b >= 2`, E2 and
+//! E4 both apply to each successor found by the ordinary double loop.
+//!
+//! # Environment
+//!
+//! * `SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME` (default off): master switch. Unset, this module's
+//!   functions are never called from `search.rs` and the successor loop is
+//!   byte-for-byte the pre-patch code.
+//! * `SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME_BUDGET` (default 4): the `b <= budget_cap` gate.
+//! * `SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME_AUDIT` (default off): builds the *unfiltered*
+//!   successor set (so the search's answer is never affected by the filters)
+//!   while also recording which successors the filters would have kept, and
+//!   checks per iteration of `Search::improve`'s fixpoint loop that the
+//!   lower-bound minimum over the kept subset equals the minimum over the
+//!   full set. A mismatch bumps the shared `FILTER_AUDIT_VIOLATIONS` counter
+//!   (the same one TIER1 / Lemma M use) and logs an error; it must always
+//!   stay 0.
+//!
+//! # Empty-admissible-set handling
+//!
+//! `Search::improve`'s fixpoint loop computes
+//! `edges.states().map(|s| s.bounds[i]).min().unwrap()`, which panics on an
+//! empty `Edges`. Before this patch that was unreachable (an unsorted set
+//! always has a non-redundant comparator), but a filter that turns out to
+//! exclude every candidate could make it reachable. Every filtered
+//! enumeration path below therefore falls back to the full unfiltered
+//! double loop whenever the filtered attempt would leave `Edges` empty, and
+//! bumps `endgame_empty_fallback`. The fallback is always sound (it is
+//! exactly the pre-patch behaviour for that one call), so it is preferred
+//! over any cleverer in-place lower-bound bookkeeping.
+
+use std::{env, iter::repeat, sync::OnceLock};
+
+use crate::output_set::{OutputSet, WVec};
+
+fn env_flag(name: &str) -> bool {
+    match env::var(name) {
+        Ok(val) => {
+            let val = val.trim().to_ascii_lowercase();
+            val == "1" || val == "true" || val == "yes"
+        }
+        Err(_) => false,
+    }
+}
+
+static ENABLED: OnceLock<bool> = OnceLock::new();
+
+/// Whether `SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME` is set, read from the environment exactly
+/// once. Default off, so an unset environment never calls into this module
+/// from `search.rs`.
+pub fn enabled() -> bool {
+    *ENABLED.get_or_init(|| env_flag("SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME"))
+}
+
+static BUDGET_CAP: OnceLock<u8> = OnceLock::new();
+
+/// `SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME_BUDGET`, read from the environment exactly once.
+/// Default 4. The filters are only consulted for a parent whose stored
+/// upper bound is `<= budget_cap()`.
+pub fn budget_cap() -> u8 {
+    *BUDGET_CAP.get_or_init(|| {
+        env::var("SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME_BUDGET")
+            .ok()
+            .and_then(|v| v.trim().parse::<u8>().ok())
+            .unwrap_or(4)
+    })
+}
+
+static AUDIT: OnceLock<bool> = OnceLock::new();
+
+/// Whether `SORTNETOPT_ENDGAME_AUDIT` is set, read from the environment
+/// exactly once. Default off. See the module doc comment for what audit
+/// mode does.
+pub fn audit_enabled() -> bool {
